  "description": "Grouped Queries with Condition",
  "code": "SELECT branch_name, AVG(balance)\n     FROM account\n     GROUP BY branch_name\n     HAVING AVG(balance) > 600;",
  "line_count": 4,
  "has_explanations": true,
  "lines": [
    {
      "line_no": 1,
      "code": "SELECT branch_name, AVG(balance)",
      "explanation": ""
    },
    {
      "line_no": 2,
      "code": "     FROM account",
      "explanation": ""
    },
    {
      "line_no": 3,
      "code": "     GROUP BY branch_name",
      "explanation": "The result data is grouped and summarized for each branch_name."
    },
    {
      "line_no": 4,
      "code": "     HAVING AVG(balance) > 600;",
      "explanation": "Just as the WHERE clause, the HAVING clause can be used to select and reject row groups. <br>As specified by 'group by', the balance data is group and subtotalled up by branch_name and then the average of subtotal balance is calculated. If the average of subtotal is greater than 600, the data is retrieved. The format of the HAVING clause parallels that of the WHERE clause, but this HAVING clause can be used as a GROUP."
    }
  ],
